IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g7-interpretation`
IMPORT `g7-art21-23-expressions`
IMPORT `g7-art24-25-powers`
IMPORT `ind-b-tests-fixtures-g7`

-- ind-b-tests-art21-25: independent tests of Articles 21 to 25 (Part 6, group G7), by test author ind-b.
-- Every expected value comes from work/ind-b/expectations.md, written from the Law before this module's imports were opened; each assertion cites its row id.
-- Commencement (Part 6 from 2019-01-01, rows E21-30, E21-31, E23-12, E23-13) is tested in ind-b-tests-commencement-vintages.l4.

§ `Article 21(1) and (2) -- "registered by the Commissioner" (rows E21-01 to E21-10, E21-36)`

-- E21-01: an unregistered Jersey company calls itself registered: contravenes 21(1); an offence under 21(10) (a level 3 fine).
#ASSERT `Art 21(1) the statement contravenes paragraph (1)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE (`ind-b7 the entity says it is` `ind-b7 registered` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Art 21(10) the statement is an offence under paragraph (10)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE FALSE (`ind-b7 the entity says it is` `ind-b7 registered` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Art 21 and 23 the penalty for the contravention` `paragraph (1) of Article 21` EQUALS (`Penalty provided` OF NOTHING, (`a fine of a level on the standard scale` 3))
-- E21-02: an unregistered foreign entity: contravenes 21(1) too.
#ASSERT `Art 21(10) the statement is an offence under paragraph (10)` `ind-b7 a foreign company` FALSE FALSE (`ind-b7 the entity says it is` `ind-b7 registered` FALSE)
-- E21-03: an unregistered EXCEPTED foreign charity: still contravenes 21(1).
#ASSERT `Art 21(10) the statement is an offence under paragraph (10)` `ind-b7 a foreign company` FALSE TRUE (`ind-b7 the entity says it is` `ind-b7 registered` TRUE)
-- E21-04: a registered charity: no contravention.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(1) the statement contravenes paragraph (1)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` TRUE (`ind-b7 the entity says it is` `ind-b7 registered` TRUE)
-- E21-05: the entity permits its agent to say so: contravenes 21(1)(b).
#ASSERT `Art 21(1) the statement contravenes paragraph (1)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE (`ind-b7 the entity lets its agent say it is` `ind-b7 registered`)
-- E21-06: a third person, knowing, intending donors to give property: contravenes 21(2); 2 years and a fine with no maximum stated.
#ASSERT `Art 21(2) the statement contravenes paragraph (2)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE (`ind-b7 a third person says it is` `ind-b7 registered` `ind-b7 aware of everything` `ind-b7 to get donations`)
#ASSERT `Art 21(9) the statement is an offence under paragraph (9)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE FALSE (`ind-b7 a third person says it is` `ind-b7 registered` `ind-b7 aware of everything` `ind-b7 to get donations`) `ind-b7 A`
#ASSERT `Art 21 and 23 the penalty for the contravention` `paragraph (2) of Article 21` EQUALS (`Penalty provided` OF (JUST 24), `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`)
-- E21-07: suspects only; intends a non-financial advantage (a free venue): contravenes 21(2) ("or other advantage").
#ASSERT `Art 21(2) the statement contravenes paragraph (2)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE (`ind-b7 a third person says it is` `ind-b7 registered` (`ind-b7 awareness` `ind-b7 suspects` `ind-b7 unaware` `ind-b7 unaware` `ind-b7 unaware`) `ind-b7 to get a free venue`)
-- E21-08: no knowledge, suspicion or grounds: no contravention.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(2) the statement contravenes paragraph (2)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE (`ind-b7 a third person says it is` `ind-b7 registered` `ind-b7 aware of nothing` `ind-b7 to get donations`)
-- E21-09: knows, but no intent: no contravention.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(2) the statement contravenes paragraph (2)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE (`ind-b7 a third person says it is` `ind-b7 registered` `ind-b7 aware of everything` `ind-b7 with no intent`)
-- E21-10: reasonable grounds to suspect; intends to mislead: contravenes.
#ASSERT `Art 21(2) the statement contravenes paragraph (2)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE (`ind-b7 a third person says it is` `ind-b7 registered` (`ind-b7 awareness` `ind-b7 has grounds` `ind-b7 unaware` `ind-b7 unaware` `ind-b7 unaware`) `ind-b7 to mislead`)
-- E21-36: the entity itself, knowing, intending donations: contravenes 21(1) and 21(2).
#ASSERT `Art 21 and 23: the contraventions made out by the statement` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE FALSE TRUE (`ind-b7 statement` `ind-b7 registered` TRUE TRUE FALSE `ind-b7 aware of everything` `ind-b7 to get donations`) `ind-b7 A` EQUALS LIST `paragraph (1) of Article 21`, `paragraph (2) of Article 21`

§ `Article 21(3) and (4) -- a Jersey entity called a "charity" (rows E21-11 to E21-19, E21-28, E21-32, E21-34)`

-- E21-11: an unregistered Jersey entity calls itself a "charity": contravenes 21(3); level 3.
#ASSERT `Art 21(3) the statement contravenes paragraph (3)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE (`ind-b7 the entity says it is` `ind-b7 charity` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Art 21 and 23 the penalty for the contravention` `paragraph (3) of Article 21` EQUALS (`Penalty provided` OF NOTHING, (`a fine of a level on the standard scale` 3))
-- E21-12: permits another to call it a "charity": contravenes 21(3)(b).
#ASSERT `Art 21(3) the statement contravenes paragraph (3)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE (`ind-b7 the entity lets its agent say it is` `ind-b7 charity`)
-- E21-13: a registered Jersey entity: no contravention.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(3) the statement contravenes paragraph (3)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` TRUE (`ind-b7 the entity says it is` `ind-b7 charity` TRUE)
-- E21-14: only about activities outside Jersey: still contravenes 21(3).
#ASSERT `Art 21(3) the statement contravenes paragraph (3)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE (`ind-b7 the entity says it is` `ind-b7 charity` FALSE)
-- E21-15: a third person, knowing both limbs, intending donations: contravenes 21(4); 2 years and a fine.
#ASSERT `Art 21(4) the statement contravenes paragraph (4)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE (`ind-b7 a third person says it is` `ind-b7 charity` `ind-b7 aware of everything` `ind-b7 to get donations`) `ind-b7 A`
#ASSERT `Art 21 and 23 the penalty for the contravention` `paragraph (4) of Article 21` EQUALS (`Penalty provided` OF (JUST 24), `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`)
-- E21-16: knows it is unregistered but not that it is a Jersey entity: no contravention.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(4) the statement contravenes paragraph (4)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE (`ind-b7 a third person says it is` `ind-b7 charity` (`ind-b7 awareness` `ind-b7 knows` `ind-b7 unaware` `ind-b7 unaware` `ind-b7 unaware`) `ind-b7 to get donations`) `ind-b7 A`
-- E21-17: knows it is a Jersey entity but believes it registered: no contravention.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(4) the statement contravenes paragraph (4)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE (`ind-b7 a third person says it is` `ind-b7 charity` (`ind-b7 awareness` `ind-b7 unaware` `ind-b7 knows` `ind-b7 unaware` `ind-b7 unaware`) `ind-b7 to get donations`) `ind-b7 A`
-- E21-18: knows both; intends only a non-financial advantage: no contravention (the wording as printed).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(4) the statement contravenes paragraph (4)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE (`ind-b7 a third person says it is` `ind-b7 charity` `ind-b7 aware of everything` `ind-b7 to get a free venue`) `ind-b7 A`
-- E21-19: reasonable grounds to suspect both; intends to mislead: contravenes.
#ASSERT `Art 21(4) the statement contravenes paragraph (4)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE (`ind-b7 a third person says it is` `ind-b7 charity` (`ind-b7 awareness` `ind-b7 has grounds` `ind-b7 has grounds` `ind-b7 unaware` `ind-b7 unaware`) `ind-b7 to mislead`) `ind-b7 A`
-- E21-28: the unregistered Jersey entity itself, knowing, intending donations: contravenes 21(3) and 21(4).
#ASSERT `Art 21 and 23: the contraventions made out by the statement` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE FALSE TRUE (`ind-b7 statement` `ind-b7 charity` TRUE TRUE FALSE `ind-b7 aware of everything` `ind-b7 to get donations`) `ind-b7 A` EQUALS LIST `paragraph (3) of Article 21`, `paragraph (4) of Article 21`
-- E21-32: an unincorporated association that is a Jersey entity by 2(3)(b): contravenes 21(3).
#ASSERT `Art 21(3) the statement contravenes paragraph (3)` (`ind-b7 entity` (LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`) TRUE) FALSE (`ind-b7 the entity says it is` `ind-b7 charity` TRUE)
-- E21-33: the same association, not a Jersey entity (no Jersey-resident governor): 21(5), not 21(3).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(3) the statement contravenes paragraph (3)` (`ind-b7 entity` (LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`) FALSE) FALSE (`ind-b7 the entity says it is` `ind-b7 charity` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Art 21(5) the statement contravenes paragraph (5)` (`ind-b7 entity` (LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`) FALSE) FALSE FALSE (`ind-b7 the entity says it is` `ind-b7 charity` TRUE)
-- E21-34: the trustees of an unregistered trust: contravene 21(3).
#ASSERT `Art 21(3) the statement contravenes paragraph (3)` (`ind-b7 entity` (LIST `the trustees of a trust`) TRUE) FALSE (`ind-b7 the entity says it is` `ind-b7 charity` TRUE)

§ `Article 21(5) to (10) -- other entities called a "charity" (rows E21-20 to E21-29, E21-35)`

-- E21-20: an unregistered US entity, not excepted, calls itself a "charity" about its Jersey activities: contravenes 21(5); level 3.
#ASSERT `Art 21(5) the statement contravenes paragraph (5)` `ind-b7 a foreign company` FALSE FALSE (`ind-b7 the entity says it is` `ind-b7 charity` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Art 21 and 23 the penalty for the contravention` `paragraph (5) of Article 21` EQUALS (`Penalty provided` OF NOTHING, (`a fine of a level on the standard scale` 3))
-- E21-21: only about activities outside Jersey: no contravention.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(5) the statement contravenes paragraph (5)` `ind-b7 a foreign company` FALSE FALSE (`ind-b7 the entity says it is` `ind-b7 charity` FALSE)
-- E21-22: an excepted foreign charity calls itself a "charity" in Jersey: neither 21(3) nor 21(5).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(5) the statement contravenes paragraph (5)` `ind-b7 a foreign company` FALSE TRUE (`ind-b7 the entity says it is` `ind-b7 charity` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(3) the statement contravenes paragraph (3)` `ind-b7 a foreign company` FALSE (`ind-b7 the entity says it is` `ind-b7 charity` TRUE)
-- E21-23: permits another to call it a "charity" about its Jersey activities: contravenes 21(5).
#ASSERT `Art 21(5) the statement contravenes paragraph (5)` `ind-b7 a foreign company` FALSE FALSE (`ind-b7 the entity lets its agent say it is` `ind-b7 charity`)
-- E21-24: a third person, knowing both limbs, intending donations: contravenes 21(6); 2 years and a fine.
#ASSERT `Art 21(6) the statement contravenes paragraph (6)` `ind-b7 a foreign company` FALSE FALSE (`ind-b7 a third person says it is` `ind-b7 charity` `ind-b7 aware of everything` `ind-b7 to get donations`) `ind-b7 A`
#ASSERT `Art 21 and 23 the penalty for the contravention` `paragraph (6) of Article 21` EQUALS (`Penalty provided` OF (JUST 24), `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`)
-- E21-25: believes it excepted, no suspicion: no contravention.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(6) the statement contravenes paragraph (6)` `ind-b7 a foreign company` FALSE FALSE (`ind-b7 a third person says it is` `ind-b7 charity` (`ind-b7 awareness` `ind-b7 knows` `ind-b7 unaware` `ind-b7 unaware` `ind-b7 unaware`) `ind-b7 to get donations`) `ind-b7 A`
-- E21-26: only about non-Jersey activities: no contravention.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(6) the statement contravenes paragraph (6)` `ind-b7 a foreign company` FALSE FALSE (`ind-b7 statement` `ind-b7 charity` FALSE FALSE FALSE `ind-b7 aware of everything` `ind-b7 to get donations`) `ind-b7 A`
-- E21-27: a non-financial advantage only: no contravention.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(6) the statement contravenes paragraph (6)` `ind-b7 a foreign company` FALSE FALSE (`ind-b7 a third person says it is` `ind-b7 charity` `ind-b7 aware of everything` `ind-b7 to get a free venue`) `ind-b7 A`
-- E21-29: a States' exception under 21(8): no contravention of (1) to (6).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(3) the statement contravenes paragraph (3)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE (`ind-b7 an excepted statement that it is` `ind-b7 charity`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(4) the statement contravenes paragraph (4)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE (`ind-b7 an excepted statement that it is` `ind-b7 charity`) `ind-b7 A`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(1) the statement contravenes paragraph (1)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE (`ind-b7 an excepted statement that it is` `ind-b7 registered`)
-- E21-29: the power is the States'.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b7 nothing is owed under` `Art 21(8) the States may prescribe exceptions`
#ASSERT `ind-b7 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE `Art 21(8) the States may prescribe exceptions` 0 (LIST EVENT `the States` `prescribe by Regulations exceptions to the prohibitions in Article 21(1) to (6)` 1))
-- E21-35: the penalties as data, all six paragraphs.
#ASSERT `Art 21 the penalty for the contravention` `paragraph (1) of Article 21` EQUALS `Art 21 the penalty for the contravention` `paragraph (5) of Article 21`
#ASSERT `Art 21 the penalty for the contravention` `paragraph (2) of Article 21` EQUALS `Art 21 the penalty for the contravention` `paragraph (6) of Article 21`

§ `Article 22 -- excepted foreign charities (rows E22-01 to E22-15)`

-- E22-01, E22-02: UK law (Scotland; England and Wales), entitled, managed from there, unregistered: excepted.
#ASSERT `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` (`ind-b7 foreign facts` `ind-b7 UK law` TRUE TRUE FALSE) FALSE
-- E22-03: managed mainly from Jersey: not excepted.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` (`ind-b7 foreign facts` `ind-b7 UK law` TRUE FALSE FALSE) FALSE
-- E22-04: not entitled to call itself a charity at home: not excepted.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` (`ind-b7 foreign facts` `ind-b7 UK law` FALSE TRUE FALSE) FALSE
-- E22-05, E22-07: Ireland or Guernsey, not prescribed: not excepted.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` (`ind-b7 foreign facts` `ind-b7 other law` TRUE TRUE FALSE) FALSE
-- E22-06, E22-12: a prescribed jurisdiction (Ireland; France, with its own word for charity): excepted.
#ASSERT `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` (`ind-b7 foreign facts` `ind-b7 prescribed law` TRUE TRUE FALSE) FALSE
-- E22-08: established under Jersey law: cannot meet the first condition.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` (`ind-b7 foreign facts` `the law of Jersey` TRUE TRUE FALSE) FALSE
-- E22-09: a registered charity: not excepted.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` (`ind-b7 foreign facts` `ind-b7 UK law` TRUE TRUE FALSE) TRUE
-- E22-10: a US entity specified in a 22(4) Order, managed from the US: excepted.
#ASSERT `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` (`ind-b7 foreign facts` `ind-b7 other law` FALSE TRUE TRUE) FALSE
-- E22-11: the same, managed mainly from Jersey: not excepted.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` (`ind-b7 foreign facts` `ind-b7 other law` FALSE FALSE TRUE) FALSE
-- E22-14, E22-15: the powers are the States' (22(5)) and the Minister's (22(4), 22(2)(a)(ii)).
#ASSERT `ind-b7 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE `Art 22(5) the States may amend the conditions` 0 (LIST EVENT `the States` `amend by Regulations the conditions of an excepted foreign charity` 1))
#ASSERT `ind-b7 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE `Art 22(4) the Minister may exempt a specified entity from the first condition` 0 (LIST EVENT `the Minister` `prescribe by Order that a specified entity is not required to meet the first condition of an excepted foreign charity` 1))
#ASSERT `ind-b7 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE `Art 22(2)(a)(ii) the Minister may prescribe a jurisdiction by Order` 0 (LIST EVENT `the Minister` `prescribe by Order a jurisdiction whose law establishes an excepted foreign charity` 1))

§ `Article 23 -- "Jersey charity" (rows E23-01 to E23-11)`

-- E23-01: a registered Jersey company managed in Jersey: may call itself a "Jersey charity".
#ASSERT NOT `Art 23(1) the statement contravenes paragraph (1)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` TRUE TRUE (`ind-b7 the entity says it is` `ind-b7 Jersey charity` TRUE)
-- E23-02: a registered charity that is not a Jersey entity: contravenes 23(1); level 3.
#ASSERT `Art 23(1) the statement contravenes paragraph (1)` `ind-b7 a foreign company` TRUE TRUE (`ind-b7 the entity says it is` `ind-b7 Jersey charity` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Art 21 and 23 the penalty for the contravention` `paragraph (1) of Article 23` EQUALS (`Penalty provided` OF NOTHING, (`a fine of a level on the standard scale` 3))
-- E23-03: managed and controlled mainly from London: contravenes.
#ASSERT `Art 23(1) the statement contravenes paragraph (1)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` TRUE FALSE (`ind-b7 the entity says it is` `ind-b7 Jersey charity` TRUE)
-- E23-04: managed from London, controlled from Jersey ("managed or controlled"): the condition is met (the caller states it).
#ASSERT `Art 23(3) the entity meets all of the conditions` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` TRUE TRUE
-- E23-05: an unregistered Jersey entity managed in Jersey: contravenes 23(1).
#ASSERT `Art 23(1) the statement contravenes paragraph (1)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE TRUE (`ind-b7 the entity says it is` `ind-b7 Jersey charity` TRUE)
-- E23-06: permits another to call it a "Jersey charity": contravenes 23(1)(b).
#ASSERT `Art 23(1) the statement contravenes paragraph (1)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE TRUE (`ind-b7 the entity lets its agent say it is` `ind-b7 Jersey charity`)
-- E23-07: a third person, knowing, intending donations: contravenes 23(2); 2 years and a fine.
#ASSERT `Art 23(2) the statement contravenes paragraph (2)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE TRUE (`ind-b7 a third person says it is` `ind-b7 Jersey charity` `ind-b7 aware of everything` `ind-b7 to get donations`) `ind-b7 A`
#ASSERT `Art 21 and 23 the penalty for the contravention` `paragraph (2) of Article 23` EQUALS (`Penalty provided` OF (JUST 24), `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`)
-- E23-08: no knowledge: no contravention.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 23(2) the statement contravenes paragraph (2)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE TRUE (`ind-b7 a third person says it is` `ind-b7 Jersey charity` `ind-b7 aware of nothing` `ind-b7 to get donations`) `ind-b7 A`
-- E23-09: a non-financial advantage only: no contravention.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 23(2) the statement contravenes paragraph (2)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE TRUE (`ind-b7 a third person says it is` `ind-b7 Jersey charity` `ind-b7 aware of everything` `ind-b7 to get a free venue`) `ind-b7 A`
-- E23-10: the entity itself, knowing, intending donations: contravenes 23(1) and 23(2) (and, being unregistered and Jersey, nothing of 21 is said: only "Jersey charity").
#ASSERT elem `paragraph (1) of Article 23` (`Art 21 and 23: the contraventions made out by the statement` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE FALSE TRUE (`ind-b7 statement` `ind-b7 Jersey charity` TRUE TRUE FALSE `ind-b7 aware of everything` `ind-b7 to get donations`) `ind-b7 A`)
#ASSERT elem `paragraph (2) of Article 23` (`Art 21 and 23: the contraventions made out by the statement` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE FALSE TRUE (`ind-b7 statement` `ind-b7 Jersey charity` TRUE TRUE FALSE `ind-b7 aware of everything` `ind-b7 to get donations`) `ind-b7 A`)
-- E23-11: a States' exception under 23(4): no contravention.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 23(1) the statement contravenes paragraph (1)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE TRUE (`ind-b7 an excepted statement that it is` `ind-b7 Jersey charity`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 23(2) the statement contravenes paragraph (2)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE TRUE (`ind-b7 an excepted statement that it is` `ind-b7 Jersey charity`) `ind-b7 A`

§ `Articles 24 and 25 -- powers (rows E24-01 to E25-04)`

-- E24-01: "charitable", by a non-registered person, soliciting from the general public: the Regulations may restrict it.
#ASSERT `Art 24(1) the use is one that the Regulations may restrict` (`ind-b7 use` "charitable" FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EMPTY
-- E24-02: "public benefit": a relevant term.
#ASSERT `Art 24(2) the term is a relevant term` "public benefit" EMPTY
-- E24-03: a related term the Regulations specify: relevant.
#ASSERT `Art 24(2) the term is a relevant term` "philanthropic" (LIST "philanthropic")
-- E24-04: "charity", even if the Regulations specify it: not a relevant term.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 24(2) the term is a relevant term` "charity" (LIST "charity")
-- E24-05: use by a registered charity: outside the power.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 24(1) the use is one that the Regulations may restrict` (`ind-b7 use` "charitable" TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EMPTY
-- E24-06: use other than in soliciting donations: outside.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 24(1) the use is one that the Regulations may restrict` (`ind-b7 use` "charitable" FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EMPTY
-- E24-07: an offence punishable by a fine (level 4, say): within the cap.
#ASSERT `Art 24(4) the penalty is no greater than a fine` (`Penalty provided` OF NOTHING, (`a fine of a level on the standard scale` 4))
-- E24-08: an offence punishable by imprisonment: outside, adapted from Articles 21 to 23 or not.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 24(4) the penalty is no greater than a fine` (`Penalty provided` OF (JUST 6), `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 24 the Regulations may attach this penalty to the offence` (`Penalty provided` OF (JUST 24), `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`) TRUE `ind-b7 A`
-- E24-09: Regulations may require the Commissioner's permission.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b7 nothing is owed under` `Art 24(3)(b) the Regulations may require permission to be sought from the Commissioner`
-- E24-10: the power is the States' (an act of the States exercises it).
#ASSERT `ind-b7 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE `Art 24(1) the States may restrict the use of a relevant term in soliciting donations` 0 (LIST EVENT `the States` `make Regulations restricting the use, other than by a registered charity, of a relevant term in soliciting donations` 1))
-- E24-11: soliciting from a prescribed description of persons: within.
#ASSERT `Art 24(1) the use is one that the Regulations may restrict` (`ind-b7 use` "charitable" FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EMPTY
-- E25-01, E25-04: the Minister's power to prescribe statements, by Order.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b7 nothing is owed under` `Art 25(1) the Minister may prescribe statements that a registered charity must make`
#ASSERT `ind-b7 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE `Art 25(1) the Minister may prescribe statements that a registered charity must make` 0 (LIST EVENT `the Minister` `prescribe by Order statements that a registered charity must make about its registration` 1))
-- E25-01: the registration number is among the statements 25(2)(a) names.
#ASSERT elem "its charity registration number" `the statements that an Order under Article 25(1) may require a charity to state (Article 25(2)(a))`

§ `Reading checks for Part 6 (expected values from each reading's own words)`

-- F7.5 B (the advantage limb harmonised): a non-financial advantage reaches 21(4) on that reading.
#ASSERT `Art 21(4) the statement contravenes paragraph (4)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE (`ind-b7 a third person says it is` `ind-b7 charity` `ind-b7 aware of everything` `ind-b7 to get a free venue`) `the interpretation with the other reading of F7.5`
-- F7.4 B (the knowing offence displaces the strict one): the entity itself, knowing: only 21(4).
#ASSERT `Art 21 and 23: the contraventions made out by the statement` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE FALSE TRUE (`ind-b7 statement` `ind-b7 charity` TRUE TRUE FALSE `ind-b7 aware of everything` `ind-b7 to get donations`) `the interpretation with the other reading of F7.4` EQUALS LIST `paragraph (4) of Article 21`
-- F7.13 B (the cap does not reach an offence adapted from Articles 21 to 23): imprisonment allowed for an adapted offence on that reading.
#ASSERT `Art 24 the Regulations may attach this penalty to the offence` (`Penalty provided` OF (JUST 24), `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`) TRUE `the interpretation with the other reading of F7.13`
-- F7.12 B (Article 22 defines the term for Article 21 only): Article 2(10)(b) gets a refusal.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity for the purpose of Article 2(10)(b)` (`ind-b7 foreign facts` `ind-b7 UK law` TRUE TRUE FALSE) FALSE `the interpretation with the other reading of F7.12`
#ASSERT `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity for the purpose of Article 2(10)(b)` (`ind-b7 foreign facts` `ind-b7 UK law` TRUE TRUE FALSE) FALSE `ind-b7 A`
-- F7.8 B (a term of 2 years is 730 days): a 731-day term from 2028-01-01 (a leap year) is within 24 months, not within 730 days.
#ASSERT `Art 21(9) and 23(7) a sentence of a number of days beginning on a day is within the maximum` 731 (YMD 2028 1 1) `ind-b7 A`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(9) and 23(7) a sentence of a number of days beginning on a day is within the maximum` 731 (YMD 2028 1 1) `the interpretation with the other reading of F7.8`

§ `Article 2(1)(ba) reached through Part 6 (row V-19)`

-- V-19 (reading A of A-09): from 2025-10-16 B is an entity under (ba) and a Jersey entity: contravenes 21(3).
#ASSERT `Art 21(3) the statement contravenes paragraph (3)` (`ind-b7 entity` (LIST `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey`) TRUE) FALSE (`ind-b7 the entity says it is` `ind-b7 charity` TRUE)


§ `Moved from ind-b-tests-disagree.l4: row V-18 of expectations.md, which failed before the repair of G7 (R2) and holds now`

-- V-18: B (an NPO body corporate under Jersey law, within none of 2(1)(c)-(h)) on 2025-10-15 is not an "entity" at all (domain.l4: kinds of entity empty), so 21(5),
-- which binds "An entity that is not a registered charity and is neither a Jersey entity nor an excepted foreign charity", does not reach it.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(5) the statement contravenes paragraph (5)` (`ind-b7 entity` EMPTY FALSE) FALSE FALSE (`ind-b7 the entity says it is` `ind-b7 charity` TRUE)
